  "problem": "Suppose we would like to find the minimum value of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}-y+z$ on the intersection of the surfaces ${y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+z=4$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\u27e82x,\\,-1,\\,1\u27e9=\\lambda \u27e80,\\,,\\,2z\u27e9+\\mu \u27e82x,\\,,\\,1\u27e9 \\\\ {y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?",
